  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_025, acc=0.635) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion. All completed experiments have used pca_n2000, so the effect of a learned RNA representation remains entirely untested. Config_037 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to a learned scVI latent (200-dim), isolating the representation effect while holding all other settings at their known-best values. This is the highest-value single-variable test: if scVI captures nonlinear gene structure better than linear PCA, it could push accuracy above 0.635; if not, we confirm PCA is sufficient and can focus remaining budget on other axes. With only 2 experiments left, testing the most impactful unexplored dimension (RNA encoder quality) on the strongest backbone is the best use of this slot."
}

